  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Campaign &amp; Advocacy Leadership Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Campaigns &amp; Advocacy Leadership Programme (CALP) has a rich history and deeply valued impact. Its objective is to increase the power and confidence of participants to lead the development and implementation of campaigning, advocacy and influencing.  Drawing on the very best practice in leading advocacy &amp; campaigns for change, the programme focuses on developing feminist facilitative leadership alongside influencing skills. So, this includes aspects such as: making systemic change happen in different contexts; building local to global connections; contributing and collaborating with multiple stakeholders, wider movements and coalitions; developing personal leadership styles and better awareness of the approaches of others; leading innovative public campaigning and influencing strategies; and effective messaging and public narrative for influencing. CALP enables participants to develop new insights to navigate through complex challenges, and to react fast, sensitively and appropriately where contexts change.</narrative>
  </description>
